`toLocaleString('en-US', ...)` produces something like "6/1/2014, 5:00:00 AM". Then `new Date(target)` parses that in local time. The diff is fractional because `this.toDate()` includes milliseconds but the target string doesn't. So diff includes fractional minutes, e.g. `-420.00205` or similar. Then `localUtcOffset - diff` is fractional. `utcOffset(offset, true)` sets `ins.$offset = offset` directly (keepLocalTime path), so `$offset` becomes fractional.

